From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omarchy-dragon-sl7 <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 19:09:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: st-vd55g: Keep the strobe GPIO off unless st,leds
 is set

The generic driver defaults sensor GPIO 1 to a strobe output when the
device tree has no 'st,leds' property, and then exposes a flash LED mode
control. On the Surface Laptop 7 the infrared illuminator (PM8550 flash,
up to 700 mA) must not be reachable from the first release, so without
'st,leds' make no GPIO a strobe output, do not create the flash LED mode
control, and guard the one place that read the control unconditionally.

Origin: ours
Upstream-Status: Not for upstream (carried as a safety default; the
        upstream driver keeps GPIO 1)
---
 drivers/media/i2c/vd55g.c | 12 +++++++-----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g.c b/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g.c
index 8c504aeef..ade2db631 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g.c
@@ -634,7 +634,7 @@ static void vd55g_get_frame_timings(struct vd55g *sensor,
 
 	timings->expo_max = timings->frame_length - VD55G_EXPO_MAX_TERM;
 
-	if (sensor->info->limit_flash_duty_cycle &&
+	if (sensor->info->limit_flash_duty_cycle && sensor->led_ctrl &&
 	    sensor->led_ctrl->val == V4L2_FLASH_LED_MODE_FLASH) {
 		timings->expo_max = timings->expo_max / 2;
 	}
@@ -2020,10 +2020,12 @@ static int vd55g_parse_dt_gpios(struct vd55g *sensor)
 		set_bit(led_gpios[i], &sensor->ext_leds_mask);
 	}
 
-	if (nb_gpios_leds == 0) {
-		sensor->gpios[1] = VD55G_GPIO_MODE_STROBE;
-		set_bit(1, &sensor->ext_leds_mask);
-	}
+	/*
+	 * Without an 'st,leds' property no GPIO is a strobe output and the
+	 * flash LED control is not created, so nothing can drive an
+	 * illuminator by accident. The generic driver used to default to
+	 * GPIO 1.
+	 */
 
 	return 0;
 }
